(:adr
  :id "D75"
  :shortcode "D75"
  :title "Universal WebAssembly Ambient Substrate, Self-Contained Micro-Binary Packaging, and Regulated Platform Leaves Standard"
  :status :active
  :date "2026-09-11"
  :cluster "architecture/runtime"
  :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "AgentScript previously utilized Rust as an intermediate compilation step to generate native binaries, imposing a 1.5 GB Cargo/LLVM toolchain burden, slow compilation cycles, and an impedance mismatch with S-expression AST semantics. Furthermore, without a formal demarcation between the core ambient runtime and specialized deployment targets, foreign toolchains threatened to contaminate developer workflows."
  :drivers [
    "WebAssembly as Ambient Substrate: The entire AgentScript core runtime, agent harness, memory ledger, and compiler must execute natively within WebAssembly (WASM/WASI)"
    "Zero-Rust Developer Distribution: The native CLI binary (asl) must be packaged as a self-contained micro-executable (<1.5 MB) via lightweight C micro-runtimes or OS-native JavaScriptCore, eliminating the Rust tax for development and distribution"
    "Regulated Platform Leaves: Rust, Go, Embedded C, SwiftUI, Jetpack Compose, and JSX are preserved and strictly regulated as peripheral, export-only targets serving specific deployment niches without imposing dependencies on the core"
    "Boundary Universalism: Unidirectional projection guarantees that adding or updating platform leaves never introduces foreign toolchain dependencies into the core ASL workspace"
  ]
  :decision "Adopt ADR-0075 (D75) establishing WebAssembly as the universal ambient substrate and primary compilation target for AgentScript. Package a minimal self-contained native binary (<1.5 MB) with zero Rust, zero Python, and zero Node dependencies. Formally regulate Rust (asl-to-rust), Go (asl-to-go), Embedded C (asl-to-c), and Polyglot VDOM UI leaves under strict unidirectional export boundaries."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D69" "D75"]
  :tasks [
    "T430WasmCoreSubstrate"
    "T430GoPlatformLeaf"
    "T430CompilerMultiTarget"
    "T430Settle"
  ]
  :consequences [
    (:pos "Eliminates the 1.5 GB Rust and LLVM toolchain burden from daily development and CI pipelines")
    (:pos "Enables true cross-platform portability across browsers, CLI, servers, and edge environments with a single WASM module")
    (:pos "Produces an ultra-compact (<1.5 MB) standalone native CLI binary with sub-2ms cold starts and <15 MB RSS")
    (:pos "Strictly regulates lateral targets (Rust, Go, C, SwiftUI, Compose, JSX) with zero toolchain bleed into the core language")
    (:neg "Requires maintaining specialized codegen emitters for lateral platform leaves")
  ])
